Subject: HAIR

As Tom pointed out in his first message on this topic, I now wear
my hair long.  For several years, it has ranged from shoulder length
to mid-back length.  But in the past I have had crew cuts, mohawks,
flat tops, braids, and shaved smooth shinhead style.  If maintenance
is what you are interested in, shinhead by far requires the lowest effor
to maintain.  Shaving takes about as long as blow-drying a full mane
but needs to be done only once a week or so.  Shampooing is unnecessary
and of course, costly conditioners are out too.  Time and financial
investment is absolutely minimized.
     But frankly, I wouldn't go back to my shiny ways because of one
simple fact that most of us do care about, namely what other people
think, especially what potential friends and lovers think.  If ease of
maintenance were the determining factor, then skin would surely be in.
But it is not the determining factor.  First impressions make an enormou
difference to who we maintain friendships.  If I were always with people
who knew me, then Maybe low maintenance would make the difference.  But
the truth is, I am as insecure about the first impression I make as the
next person, and so are you.
Rob Michels  michels@unc.bitnet

